# `legion/settings.py` lists this directory in STATICFILES_DIRS, and Django
# raises staticfiles.W004 for an entry that does not exist - so on a fresh
# clone, before anyone has run `npm run build`, `manage.py check` would report
# an issue about a directory that is simply empty on purpose. This file is what
# keeps the directory in git; `server/.gitignore` excludes its only real
# content, `app/`, because that is build output.
